So annoying, sigh...

313
00:26:34,749 --> 00:26:36,449
どいつもこいつもそいつもあいつも
This one, that one, that guy, this guy...

314
00:26:36,449 --> 00:26:38,149
意味わかんねえ！
Makes no sense at all!

315
00:26:38,149 --> 00:26:39,649
どうしたって どう見たって
No matter what, however you look at it,

316
00:26:39,649 --> 00:26:41,049
損したって問題渋滞
even at a loss, it's a gridlock of problems.

317
00:26:41,049 --> 00:26:42,649
それでもあっちこっちそっちぼっち
Still, over here, over there, all alone,

318
00:26:42,649 --> 00:26:44,249
マジZ世代 猿も欲しがる
totally Gen Z, even monkeys crave it.

319
00:26:44,249 --> 00:26:45,649
パンチライン欲しいの
"I want a punchline,"

320
00:26:45,649 --> 00:26:47,149
意味とかどっちだっていいよ
"I don't care what it means either way,"

321
00:26:47,149 --> 00:26:48,649
歌詞とかどうでもいいので
"the lyrics don't matter at all,"

322
00:26:48,649 --> 00:26:50,649
伸びるのをください
"just give me something that goes viral."

323
00:26:50,649 --> 00:26:53,449
さあ皆で笑いましょう
Come on, let's all laugh together.

324
00:26:53,449 --> 00:26:56,449
芸術より数なんでしょう？
It's all about the numbers over art, right?

325
00:26:56,449 --> 00:26:59,549
ウイルスに酷い代償
A terrible price paid to the virus.

326
00:26:59,549 --> 00:27:01,649
じゃあどうすんの？それでいいんだっけ？
So what now? Was that really okay?

327
00:27:01,649 --> 00:27:05,449
頭は空回り死んでいく
My head spins in circles, slowly dying.

328
00:27:06,949 --> 00:27:08,649
ふざけるな！
Don't screw with me!

329
00:27:08,649 --> 00:27:11,049
バイバイ バズメロディ
Bye-bye, buzz melody.

330
00:27:11,049 --> 00:27:13,649
疑えよ 大概 嘘ばかり
Doubt it all, it's mostly lies anyway.

331
00:27:13,649 --> 00:27:17,049
化けんな 幻想でも理想でもいい
Don't disguise yourself—illusions or ideals, both are fine.

332
00:27:17,049 --> 00:27:19,949
君の歌いたかったもんはどうしたんだい？
What happened to what you wanted to sing?

333
00:27:19,949 --> 00:27:22,849
このままじゃ到底 終われない
We can't possibly end it like this.

334
00:27:22,849 --> 00:27:25,849
欲しいのはきっとお金じゃない
What we want surely isn't money.

335
00:27:25,849 --> 00:27:29,249
負けんな 覚醒せよ鼓動たちよ
Don't lose, awaken, our heartbeats!

336
00:27:29,249 --> 00:27:31,849
君の歌いたかったものがきっとあるんだ
There's surely something you wanted to sing.

337
00:27:31,849 --> 00:27:33,449
ふざけるな…
Don't screw with me...

338
00:27:33,449 --> 00:27:36,849
ふざけるな！バイバイ バズメロディ
Don't screw with me! Bye-bye, buzz melody.

339
00:27:36,849 --> 00:27:39,749
疑えよ 大概 嘘ばかり
Doubt it all, it's mostly lies anyway.

340
00:27:39,749 --> 00:27:43,049
化けんな 幻想でも理想でもいい
Don't disguise yourself—illusions or ideals, both are fine.

341
00:27:43,049 --> 00:27:45,849
君の歌いたかったもんはどうしたんだい？
What happened to what you wanted to sing?

342
00:27:45,849 --> 00:27:48,649
無様でもオールライ 嘘じゃない
Even if it's clumsy, it's alright—it's not a lie.

343
00:27:48,649 --> 00:27:51,749
お金や理想で満たす前に
Before filling yourself with money or ideals,

344
00:27:51,749 --> 00:27:54,949
負けんな 覚醒せよ鼓動たちよ
don't lose, awaken, our heartbeats!

345
00:27:54,949 --> 00:27:57,849
僕の伝えたかったもんはどうしたんだい？
What happened to what I wanted to convey?

346
00:27:57,849 --> 00:27:59,649
意味わかんねえ！
Makes no sense at all!

347
00:27:59,649 --> 00:28:01,649
意味わかんねえよ！
It makes no damn sense!

348
00:28:01,649 --> 00:28:04,449
Oh...

349
00:28:23,449 --> 00:28:25,449
意味わかんねえ！
Makes no sense at all!

350
00:28:34,749 --> 00:28:35,949
せーの！
Ready, set...

351
00:28:35,949 --> 00:28:40,949
沙花叉、お誕生日おめでとーー！
Sakamata, happy birthday--!

352
00:28:40,949 --> 00:28:43,449
ありがとーー！
Thank you so much--!

353
00:28:43,449 --> 00:28:45,449
おめでとー！やったー！
Congrats! Woohoo!

354
00:28:45,449 --> 00:28:46,949
何歳になったわけ？
So how old did you turn?

355
00:28:46,949 --> 00:28:48,649
20歳バージョン2！
20 years old, version 2!

356
00:28:48,649 --> 00:28:50,949
おー！いいね！バージョン2！
Ooh! Nice! Version 2!

357
00:28:50,949 --> 00:28:52,949
ありがとー！
Thank you!

358
00:28:52,949 --> 00:28:55,949
ちょっとみんなせっかく来てくれ…あっ…
Guys, thank you so much for coming... Ah...

359
00:28:55,949 --> 00:28:59,449
おい！大丈夫？倒れてる！
Hey! Are you okay? She collapsed!

360
00:28:59,449 --> 00:29:01,949
あんた違うでしょ！何番前や？
You're not the one! Whose turn was that?

361
00:29:02,949 --> 00:29:05,949
だけど、今日の主役ですから、水生生物は！
But hey, the aquatic creature is today's star!

362
00:29:05,949 --> 00:29:08,949
じゃあみんなに一言言ってね、去ってもらおうかなって！
So I figured everyone could say a few words before heading off!

363
00:29:08,949 --> 00:29:11,449
1人ずつ来なよ、ほら。スムーズにほら、愛をね。
Come up one by one, come on. Smoothly share some love.

364
00:29:11,449 --> 00:29:13,949
一言愛をね！一言言いに来なよ、ほら。
A quick word of love! Come say a few words, go on.

365
00:29:13,949 --> 00:29:15,949
じゃあ誰から？ほら、嫌…
Alright, who's first? Look, if you don't...

366
00:29:15,949 --> 00:29:18,449
うん… ママだよ。
Yeah... It's your mama.

367
00:29:18,449 --> 00:29:21,449
おめでと！ありがと！
Congrats! Thank you!

368
00:29:21,449 --> 00:29:24,449
何それ？！何この動き？！何あいつ！
What is that?! What's with that move?! What is she doing?!

369
00:29:24,449 --> 00:29:26,949
もう、ほら、ちゃんときなよ！
Geez, come on, do it properly!

370
00:29:26,949 --> 00:29:29,949
はいはい。変な人いて怖かったでしょ？
Okay, okay. That weird person was scary, wasn't she?

371
00:29:28,949 --> 00:29:30,949
なんかおかしくね？
Isn't something off here?

372
00:29:29,949 --> 00:29:32,449
ママよ。
I'm your mama.

373
00:29:30,949 --> 00:29:33,949
あー違うよ！違う、違う！
Ah, no, that's wrong! No, no!

374
00:29:33,949 --> 00:29:36,449
押し戻した！おい！ちょっと待って！
She pushed her back! Hey! Wait a sec!

375
00:29:36,449 --> 00:29:39,949
俺がママだ！俺がママだ！
I'm the mama! I'm the mama!

376
00:29:39,949 --> 00:29:44,449
待って、ちょっと待って！あの、別にうちら芸人じゃないのよ！
Wait, hold on a second! Look, we're not comedians!

377
00:29:44,449 --> 00:29:46,449
手招きしてたからびびった。
You were beckoning, so it startled me.

378
00:29:46,449 --> 00:29:49,949
はい！これからもクロヱお姉ちゃんに頼ってね〜！
Yes! Rely on big sis Chloe from now on too, okay~?

379
00:29:49,949 --> 00:29:52,949
お姉ちゃんだと思ってるの？本当に。
Do you honestly think you're my big sister?

380
00:29:52,949 --> 00:29:55,449
おかしい！おかしいよ！
That's crazy! That's so uncalled for!

381
00:29:55,449 --> 00:29:58,949
ほら、ちゃんと愛をね！最後愛を！スムーズにね！
Come on, give some love properly! Love at the end! Smoothly!

382
00:29:58,949 --> 00:30:01,949
いや、でも、うちらの、ズッ友の仲やんか。
Well, but aren't we lifelong besties?

383
00:30:01,449 --> 00:30:02,949
そうね！
That's right!

384
00:30:02,449 --> 00:30:04,249
だから、せーのって言ったら…
So, when I say "Ready, set..."

385
00:30:03,606 --> 00:30:04,806
分かるよな？
You know what to do, right?

386
00:30:04,806 --> 00:30:06,006
分かった。行くよ？
Got it. Here we go!

387
00:30:06,306 --> 00:30:09,006
せーの、スリー、ツー、ワン！
Ready, set... Three, two, one!

388
00:30:09,406 --> 00:30:11,006
待って！待って！
Wait! Hold on!

389
00:30:11,006 --> 00:30:12,706
全然違う！
You're completely out of sync!

390
00:30:12,706 --> 00:30:13,506
いや、合わせて！
No, match with me!

391
00:30:13,506 --> 00:30:14,106
合わせて！
Match with me!

392
00:30:14,106 --> 00:30:16,806
せーの、スリー・サイコー！
Ready, set... Three, awesome!

393
00:30:19,106 --> 00:30:21,106
ハート作って！これでいいんだよ！
Make a heart! Like this is fine!

394
00:30:21,106 --> 00:30:23,106
大丈夫？届いてる？
Is this okay? Are we reaching you?

395
00:30:24,106 --> 00:30:26,806
じゃあね、みんな！ありがとう！
See ya, everyone! Thank you!

396
00:30:26,806 --> 00:30:31,106
ありがとう！頑張って！応援してるよ！
Thank you! Good luck! We're rooting for you!

397
00:30:31,106 --> 00:30:33,406
ママ、良かったよ！
Mama, you were great!

398
00:30:33,606 --> 00:30:36,406
よしよしよし...
There, there, there...

399
00:30:36,406 --> 00:30:38,806
ありがとう！バイバーイ！
Thank you! Bye-bye!

400
00:30:38,806 --> 00:30:40,806
頑張れー！さいならー！
Do your best! Farewell!

401
00:30:41,006 --> 00:30:42,706
なんかうるさかったな。
That was kinda noisy...

402
00:30:42,706 --> 00:30:44,606
頑張るか。よし。
Alright, let's do this. Okay!

403
00:30:52,606 --> 00:30:56,306
くだらない愛の結果で
As the outcome of a pointless love,

404
00:30:56,306 --> 00:30:59,306
僕らは生まれ落ちて
we were born into this world,

405
00:30:59,306 --> 00:31:03,806
呼吸さえ強いられているけど
forced even to keep breathing, but...

406
00:31:04,606 --> 00:31:07,506
綺麗な言葉並べて
Lining up pretty words,

407
00:31:07,506 --> 00:31:10,406
醜さに蓋をして
putting a lid over the ugliness,

408
00:31:10,406 --> 00:31:14,106
自分を愛せないままだな
I still can't bring myself to love who I am...

409
00:31:14,806 --> 00:31:16,806
ずっと
Not for the longest time.

410
00:31:19,606 --> 00:31:24,606
波に名前をつけること、僕らの呼吸に終わりがあること。
[Song: Naming the Waves, Our Breathing Having an End - Tatsuya Kitani]

411
00:31:27,406 --> 00:31:30,806
くだらない嘘を言う度
Every time a pointless lie is told,

412
00:31:30,806 --> 00:31:34,106
青い色 こぼれ落ちた
shades of blue came spilling down,

413
00:31:34,106 --> 00:31:38,106
硝子の瞳が綺麗で
and those glassy eyes were so beautiful.

414
00:31:38,906 --> 00:31:42,306
君のその瞼の様に
Just like those eyelids of yours,

415
00:31:42,306 --> 00:31:45,106
優しい人になってさ
if I could become a kind person,

416
00:31:45,106 --> 00:31:49,406
そんな僕を愛したいんだよ
I would want to love that version of myself.

417
00:31:50,106 --> 00:31:56,006
私の呼吸に終わりがあること
Knowing that there is an end to my breath,

418
00:31:56,006 --> 00:32:00,406
君の声を覚えている
I still remember your voice.

419
00:32:00,906 --> 00:32:04,206
生まれては消えていくこと
Being born only to fade away,

420
00:32:04,206 --> 00:32:07,306
それだけを繰り返している
repeating that over and over again.

421
00:32:07,306 --> 00:32:10,306
僕らがもし また会えたらだなんて
"What if we could meet again?"

422
00:32:10,306 --> 00:32:12,606
思ってた
I used to think.

423
00:32:13,106 --> 00:32:16,606
生まれては消えて行くだけの
Merely being born only to fade away,

424
00:32:16,606 --> 00:32:19,806
青白い波に名前をつけることに
giving a name to these pale blue waves...

425
00:32:19,806 --> 00:32:24,106
意味は無かったのかな、なんてさ
Was there truly no meaning to it at all?

426
00:32:44,606 --> 00:32:47,806
他愛ない急ぎ足見た
I watched trivial, hurried footsteps,

427
00:32:47,806 --> 00:32:50,606
積み木で遊んでいる
playing with building blocks,

428
00:32:50,606 --> 00:32:55,106
崩れるその日を待ってる
waiting for the day they collapse.

429
00:32:55,606 --> 00:32:59,006
澄み切った夜の静寂
In the crystal-clear silence of the night,

430
00:32:59,006 --> 00:33:02,106
君の頬の赤い色で
with the rosy flush on your cheeks,

431
00:33:02,106 --> 00:33:06,406
もうすぐ桜が咲くだろう
the cherry blossoms will surely bloom soon.

432
00:33:07,406 --> 00:33:13,006
僕らの呼吸に意味がなくても
Even if there is no meaning to our breathing,

433
00:33:13,006 --> 00:33:17,606
二人はまた恋をする
the two of us will fall in love once more.

434
00:33:18,106 --> 00:33:21,406
生まれては消えていくこと
Being born only to fade away,

435
00:33:21,406 --> 00:33:24,406
それだけを繰り返している
repeating that over and over again.

436
00:33:24,406 --> 00:33:29,806
そして君も 夜の海に帰って行くんだろう
And you too will likely return to the night sea.

437
00:33:30,106 --> 00:33:33,606
生まれては消えて行くだけの
Merely being born only to fade away,

438
00:33:33,606 --> 00:33:36,806
青白い波に名前をつけることに
giving a name to these pale blue waves...

439
00:33:36,806 --> 00:33:40,106
囚われている
I am still trapped by it.

440
00:33:40,406 --> 00:33:43,606
覚えているかな
Do you remember?

441
00:33:43,606 --> 00:33:47,306
いつかの春の朝に
On a spring morning back then,

442
00:33:47,306 --> 00:33:50,606
桜の木の下で
under the cherry blossom tree,

443
00:33:50,606 --> 00:33:56,106
約束したこと
what we promised each other.

444
00:33:58,106 --> 00:34:02,106
思い出も 君の名前も
Both the memories and your name,

445
00:34:02,106 --> 00:34:04,606
いつの日か失ってしまって
one day I will lose them all,

446
00:34:04,606 --> 00:34:09,606
僕もいつか この海と一つになるんだろう
and I too will someday become one with this sea.

447
00:34:10,106 --> 00:34:13,606
君のいない冬の空気が
As the winter air without you

448
00:34:13,606 --> 00:34:16,406
僕の頬を刺す その痛みさえ
stings my cheek, even that pain

449
00:34:16,406 --> 00:34:18,606
愛していたい
is something I want to love.

450
00:34:18,606 --> 00:34:21,806
生まれては消えていくこと
Being born only to fade away,

451
00:34:21,806 --> 00:34:24,806
それだけを繰り返している
repeating that over and over again.

452
00:34:24,806 --> 00:34:28,106
僕らがもし また会えたらだなんて
"What if we could meet again?"

453
00:34:28,106 --> 00:34:30,406
思ってた
I used to think.

454
00:34:30,406 --> 00:34:33,906
生まれては消えて行くだけの
Merely being born only to fade away,

455
00:34:33,906 --> 00:34:37,106
青白い波に名前をつけることに
giving a name to these pale blue waves...

456
00:34:37,106 --> 00:34:41,806
意味は無かったのかな
Was there truly no meaning to it at all?

457
00:34:42,606 --> 00:34:48,106
こうして冬が終わって
And like this, winter comes to an end,

458
00:34:48,606 --> 00:34:53,606
青い春が来る
and a blue spring arrives.

459
00:35:39,390 --> 00:35:41,390
UNHAPPY? 悩める人の子よ
Unhappy? O troubled child of man,

460
00:35:41,490 --> 00:35:43,290
UNLUCKY? 人成らざる者も
Unlucky? Even you non-human beings,

461
00:35:43,390 --> 00:35:45,290
BE HAPPY! 弛まず目指せよ
Be happy! Strive tirelessly for it,

462
00:35:45,390 --> 00:35:46,590
生きているんだし
after all, you're alive.

463
00:35:46,690 --> 00:35:48,290
目を逸らした過去も
The past you averted your eyes from,

464
00:35:48,390 --> 00:35:49,890
退屈な未来も
and the boring future too—

465
00:35:49,990 --> 00:35:50,790
カウンセリング
counseling!

466
00:35:50,890 --> 00:35:52,890
やれやれ 古今東西 ピースピース
Good grief, everywhere and through all time, peace peace!

467
00:35:52,990 --> 00:35:54,090
UNHAPPY

468
00:35:54,390 --> 00:35:55,590
UNLUCKY

469
00:35:56,090 --> 00:35:57,390
BE HAPPY!

470
00:35:57,590 --> 00:36:00,090
UNDEAD

471
00:36:05,490 --> 00:36:10,090
ね、ね、ね、ね 何だかどうして 戦ってるようなそんな気がするの
Hey, hey, hey, hey, why does it somehow feel like I'm fighting?

472
00:36:10,390 --> 00:36:13,590
触れられない (触れたくもない) 過去の自分自分自分自分と
With the past me, me, me, me, untouchable (and unwanted to touch).

473
00:36:13,690 --> 00:36:16,490
もうとっくに死んでる 透明な亡霊と対決
Facing off against a transparent ghost that died long ago,

474
00:36:16,590 --> 00:36:19,390
幼気で痛い記憶の奥
deep within childish, painful memories.

475
00:36:19,490 --> 00:36:21,690
残念? もう居ないのに
Regret? Even though they're already gone...

476
00:36:21,790 --> 00:36:23,590
あれ? そっちが良い? アイロニーね
Huh? That's better? How ironic.

477
00:36:23,690 --> 00:36:26,690
透かされているのは現在の自分?
Is the one being seen through my present self?

478
00:36:26,790 --> 00:36:28,790
ナンセンス 消えないレッテル YES
Nonsense, an indelible label, yes!

479
00:36:28,890 --> 00:36:31,590
要はコンプレックス 取り憑かれているみたい
In short, a complex—it's like I'm possessed.

480
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:34,790
巻き付いたまま まだ離れない
Still wrapped around me, refusing to let go,

481
00:36:34,890 --> 00:36:38,090
在りし日の自分
the self from days gone by.

482
00:36:38,290 --> 00:36:39,790
UNDEAD

483
00:36:39,890 --> 00:36:42,390
死んじゃない お前とお前の連鎖
Not dead yet—a chain connecting you with yourself.

484
00:36:42,490 --> 00:36:46,390
生きていることとは 変わり続けることだ
To be alive is to keep on changing!

485
00:36:46,490 --> 00:36:49,390
不幸に甘んじて 満足するなよ
Don't settle for unhappiness and be satisfied!

486
00:36:49,490 --> 00:36:53,190
幸せになろうとしないなんて 卑怯だ
Not even trying to become happy is just cowardly!

487
00:36:53,290 --> 00:36:56,390
この世 この世は 奇怪奇怪ファンタジー
This world, this world is a bizarre, bizarre fantasy.

488
00:36:56,490 --> 00:36:59,490
次は鬼が出るか 蛇が出るか
Will an ogre or a serpent appear next?

489
00:36:59,590 --> 00:37:02,590
出会って遭って やっと始まる物語
Encountering and facing them, the story finally begins!

490
00:37:02,690 --> 00:37:04,590
